<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Elizabeth Aldridge — A human perspective on analytics</title><meta name="description" content="Elizabeth Aldridge. Business analytics, human-centered AI, and a little curiosity. University of Arkansas, graduating Summer 2027."><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a href="#" class="wordmark">ELIZABETH ALDRIDGE</a><span class="header-note">ANALYTICS, WITH A HUMAN PERSPECTIVE.</span><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#projects">Projects</a><a href="links.html">Quick links</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section class="opening" id="about"><h1><span>ABOUT</span><span>ME</span></h1><div class="intro-grid"><figure class="photo"><img src="headshot.png" alt="Professional headshot of Elizabeth Aldridge" width="1254" height="1254" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><figcaption>A LITTLE CURIOSITY. A LOT OF POSSIBILITY.</figcaption></figure><div class="bio"><p class="small">THE PERSON BEHIND THE ANALYSIS</p><h2>ELIZABETH<br>ALDRIDGE</h2><p class="role-label">BUSINESS ANALYTICS & AI</p><div class="rule"></div><p>I’m an Information Systems graduate and Master of Applied Business Analytics student focused on practical AI applications and business decision-making.</p><p>My experience brings together generative AI experimentation, dashboards, data mining, and enterprise technology evaluation—with a practical understanding of training, customer service, and process improvement.</p><p class="handwritten">Making sense of data.<br>Making space for people.</p><a class="text-link" href="#projects">Explore my projects</a></div></div><div class="notes-row"><div class="inspired"><p class="small">GROUNDED IN</p><p>INFORMATION SYSTEMS.<br>BUSINESS ANALYTICS.<br>A HUMAN PERSPECTIVE.</p></div><aside class="paper-note"><h3>Currently</h3><p>STUDYING AT THE UNIVERSITY OF ARKANSAS<br>EXPLORING PRACTICAL AI<br>GRADUATING SUMMER 2027</p></aside><p class="margin-note">An analytical mind,<br>an open notebook.</p></div></section><section class="projects section" id="projects"><div class="section-top"><p class="small">01 / SELECTED CLASS PROJECTS</p><span class="handwritten">Ideas into interfaces.</span></div><h2 class="section-title">Learning through<br>the <em>making.</em></h2><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">AI-ASSISTED PORTFOLIO DEVELOPMENT</span><h3>A portfolio,<br>shaped by AI.</h3><p class="caption">CHATGPT · GOOGLE STITCH</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Turning design feedback into a live portfolio.</p><p>I experimented with ChatGPT and Google Stitch to develop a live portfolio and a mobile link page. I directed AI outputs through prompts, design feedback, and iterative refinement.</p></div></article><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">GLOBAL INEQUALITY ANALYSIS</span><h3>Patterns in<br>global inequality.</h3><p class="caption">SAS ENTERPRISE MINER · EXCEL</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Using data mining to examine global inequality.</p><p>I prepared data in Excel and contributed to a SAS data-mining workflow using StatExplore and regression. I documented the methods and findings in a group report.</p></div></article><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">RESOLVEFORWARD PILOT EVALUATION</span><h3>A clearer view<br>of service.</h3><p class="caption">POWER BI · DAX</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Evaluating service performance through an interactive dashboard.</p><p>I built Power BI visuals, KPIs, slicers, and DAX measures to evaluate service performance. I compared segments and communicated a pilot recommendation, limitations, and review criteria.</p></div></article><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">ENTERPRISE TECHNOLOGY EVALUATION</span><h3>Evaluating<br>SAP HANA Cloud.</h3><p class="caption">ENTERPRISE SYSTEMS COURSEWORK</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Connecting technology choices with business needs.</p><p>I evaluated SAP HANA Cloud against an on-premises environment and prepared a management recommendation addressing scalability, pricing, integration, and proof-of-concept testing.</p></div></article><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">BLUEBOX KIOSK RENTAL SYSTEM</span><h3>BlueBox</h3><p class="caption">C# · ASP.NET CORE · SQL SERVER</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Building a rental system around business requirements.</p><p>I built a kiosk rental system using C# ASP.NET Core and SQL Server, applying relational database design and SQL to business requirements and external data.</p></div></article><article class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">STASHFLOW PORTFOLIO TRACKER</span><h3>StashFlow</h3><p class="caption">C# · ASP.NET CORE · SQL SERVER</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Contributing to a team portfolio-tracking application.</p><p>I developed the investment form and contributed sprint backlogs, design diagrams, and demo test data for a team portfolio-tracking application.</p></div></article></section><section class="experience section" id="experience"><div class="section-top"><p class="small">02 / EXPERIENCE</p><span class="handwritten">From the everyday.</span></div><h2 class="section-title">A closer look<br>at the <em>work.</em></h2><div class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">HIDEAWAY PIZZA · MAY 2026–PRESENT</span><h3>Service through<br>collaboration.</h3><p class="caption">SERVER<br>ROGERS, ARKANSAS</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Accuracy and teamwork in a busy service environment.</p><p>I manage competing customer requests accurately and coordinate with coworkers to resolve issues and support daily service.</p></div></div><div class="work-grid"><div class="work-heading"><span class="small">PALM BEACH TAN · AUGUST 2024–MAY 2026</span><h3>Finding clarity<br>in the details.</h3><p class="caption">ASSISTANT MANAGER<br>SPRINGDALE, ARKANSAS</p></div><div class="work-copy"><p class="lead">Organized information, thoughtful training, and better follow-up.</p><p>I replaced sticky-note tracking with a structured employee and customer issue log to organize records and support consistent follow-up.</p><p>I analyzed sales and inventory trends and used operational reporting to support inventory, staffing, and business decisions.</p><p>I trained employees using a 21-day guide, added manager notes, and organized sales competitions to support product knowledge, sales skills, and consistent procedures.</p></div></div></section><section class="perspective section"><div class="section-top"><p class="small">03 / PERSPECTIVE</p><span class="small">TECHNOLOGY. PEOPLE. POSSIBILITY.</span></div><div class="perspective-grid"><h2 class="section-title">A human side<br>to <em>AI.</em></h2><div><p class="lead">I want to help people work with AI—and feel confident doing it.</p><p>I’m interested in making AI easier to understand, supporting hands-on learning, and helping organizations adopt tools that are useful in real work. I’m also interested in contributing to building and improving AI models.</p><p>My background in Information Systems, Business Analytics, and Marketing shapes how I approach that goal: with technical curiosity and attention to the people using the technology.</p></div></div><div class="education"><div><p class="small">NOW / EXPECTED SUMMER 2027</p><h3>Master of Applied Business Analytics</h3><p>Graduate studies · University of Arkansas</p></div><div><p class="small">FOUNDATION / MAY 2026</p><h3>BSBA, Information Systems</h3><p>Business Analytics concentration · Marketing minor<br>University of Arkansas</p></div></div></section><section class="toolkit section"><div class="section-top"><p class="small">04 / THE TOOLKIT</p><span class="handwritten">Always learning.</span></div><h2 class="section-title">What I bring<br>to the <em>table.</em></h2><div class="skills"><article><h3>Analysis</h3><p>Python · JupyterLab · SQL · Excel<br>Power BI · DAX · Tableau<br>SAS Enterprise Miner · KPI analysis</p></article><article><h3>AI & productivity</h3><p>ChatGPT · Claude · Gemini · Copilot<br>NotebookLM · Muse · Notion<br>Loom · Gamma</p></article><article><h3>Development</h3><p>C# · ASP.NET Core · SQL Server · T-SQL<br>Visual Studio · VS Code · Cursor<br>Replit · GitHub</p></article><article><h3>Design & prototyping</h3><p>Google Stitch · Figma · FigJam<br>Canva · Pen.dev · Excalidraw · tldraw</p></article><article><h3>Enterprise systems</h3><p>SAP ERPsim · SAP HANA Cloud</p></article><article><h3>Business & people</h3><p>Technology evaluation · Reporting<br>Employee training · Customer service<br>Process improvement</p></article></div></section><section class="contact section" id="contact"><div class="section-top"><p class="small">THE NEXT CHAPTER</p><span class="small">OPEN TO OPPORTUNITIES NATIONWIDE · SUMMER 2027</span></div><h2>LET’S<br><em>connect.</em></h2><div class="contact-bottom"><p>Exploring opportunities in business analytics<br>and AI consulting after graduation.</p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/elizabeth-aldridge-2256142a5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link">Find me on LinkedIn</a></div></section></main><footer><span>© 2026 Elizabeth Aldridge</span><a href="#">Back to top</a></footer></body></html>

